# Password Spray Investigation Case Study

> **Portfolio Disclaimer:** This is a simulated SOC investigation created for educational and portfolio purposes. It does not contain production data, real credentials, or confidential information.

## Executive Summary

A Microsoft Sentinel detection identified repeated failed authentication attempts originating from a single IP address and targeting multiple user accounts.

The activity was investigated as a potential password spray attack. The investigation focused on determining the number of targeted accounts, checking for successful authentications, reviewing the source IP address, and identifying any related suspicious activity.

